direct-colourless-val
owner: fable-5.1 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-16
what: the operator's ask, after measuring: inside a direct block
  `val x = fetch(k)` with no mark and no ascription INFERS the program
  type, so the colouring conversion fires at each USE, not at the
  declaration — `val` and `lazy val` both silently degrade to `def`
  (measured: `val, val, lazy val, lazy val, def, def` where the
  ascribed spelling gives `val, lazy val, def, def`). Make the words
  mean what they say with no `!` and no ascription: a val whose rhs is
  a program of the block and whose uses are COLOURED becomes a binding
  (by value), a lazy val becomes the Once cell (by need), a def stays
  by name. A val used as a PROGRAM (passed on, marked) is untouched;
  one used both ways is refused with both readings named.
files: src/main/scala/Direct.scala, src/test/scala/TestDirectOnce.scala,
  docs/direct-style.md, CHANGELOG.md
